      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Pioneers from Connecticut first settled Edwardsville in 1768 during the Susquehanna Company’s expansion.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edwardsville%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1889, the Bartels Brewing Company opened, becoming a regional brewing powerhouse in Northeastern Pennsylvania.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edwardsville%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Edwardsville once hosted a vital electric trolley stop, linking residents to Wilkes-Barre and Kingston.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edwardsville%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Susquehanna River forms Edwardsville’s southern border, shaping its early transportation routes.",
